cial and retail center, residents will benefit from added convenience with dining, daily necessities, and lifestyle amenities just a short walk away upon completion.\nEnveloped by international schools, healthcare facilities, parks, cafés, and supermarkets, Desa ParkCity is renowned for its lush greenery, pedestrian-friendly atmosphere, and vibrant community living.\nWith strong demand and limited new supply in the vicinity, many buyers are purchasing units ahead of completion to lock in current prices. As the project approaches handover and commercial activities ramp up, there is substantial potential for both rental yields and capital growth.\nReserve your unit today before completion and price changes take effect. Contact me for further information.\nGrace Ho | REN 02063 | 0*****\n\n## Noora\n\nNoora (also styled as Noöra) is a freehold serviced residence poised to become a landmark integrated development within the award-winning Desa ParkCity township in Kuala Lumpur. Developed by ParkCity Group, this project embodies a Scandinavian design ethos, emphasizing light, simplicity, and a seamless connection with nature. Launched in November 2022 and slated for completion in 2026, Noora integrates residential living with the convenience of on-site retail, offering a wholesome and balanced lifestyle. Noora stands on a 6.63-acre plot and consists of two 52-storey towers that house a total of 1,156 residential units. The development's name, meaning \"light\" in Scandinavian languages, is reflected in its light-filled architecture and airy, open spaces. At its base, Noora features \"Noora Walk,\" a three-storey, 50,000 sq ft retail component managed by the developer, designed to host a curated selection of tenants including grocers and eateries for ultimate convenience. "
